.SH NAME
le - See and stop what's listening on localhost


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBle [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
le — a fast, keyboard-driven view of localhost listeners, with the
smarts to stop each the right way (TERM, brew services, docker, or
launchctl bootout).

.PP
The rule underneath every stop: identity must be proven, twice. le
re-verifies the PID's start time immediately before signalling, so a
recycled PID never gets a signal meant for something else — and when
identity can't be proven, le refuses rather than guesses. That is
the difference from \fBlsof | kill\fR\&.

.PP
Run with no arguments to open the live TUI.

.PP
Exit codes: 0 success · 1 failure · 2 usage error · 124 --timeout elapsed.


